{"author":{"id":"5698b6d16d951325374257d86a2e673da0e55970c3d21c0f7c6f49018f24e5bf"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1786429031,"nonce":"UqT98hBA93D8+7rQfiJoqM/4bfA=","message":"Resolved as option (A): the field is gone from the write path and the column is dropped (00038_reconciler_is_not_optional.sql). reconcile_interval_s stays fully tunable; on/off does not exist. ADR 0006's status restored, with the 2026-08-08 amendment marked SUPERSEDED (kept verbatim) and a new amendment recording why.\n\nThe red team falsified the previous amendment's OWN claims, which is what decided it:\n1. The warning never reached a human. withReconcileWarning was called only from sources/service.Health; GET /api/v1/sources builds rows in api.decorate straight off HealthFor and never passed through it — so 'on every row of GET /api/v1/sources' was false. And no file under web/ reads health.warnings at all, so 'the UI renders warnings already' was false too. There was no UI toggle; the only way to set the flag was a hand-written API call and the only way to find out was another one.\n2. The flag did not do the thing it was kept for. The amendment kept it for the firewalled deployment, arguing that without it such a source goes unreachable and freezes the reaper forever. True — and equally true WITH it: a source oto cannot reach never earns a healthy row, Create seeds unknown, and unknown blocks the reaper exactly as unreachable does. The firewalled deployment's expiry was frozen either way.\n\nEvery other candidate need falls to reconcile_interval_s (10s-3600s): rate limits, slow or distant AM, a cluster with no silences (reconciliation still does divergence accounting, missed-webhook recovery, send_resolved discovery and route-timing observation).\n\nA finding the issue missed, and the important one: source_health.status has only two writers (manual Probe and the reconcile pass) — TouchPush explicitly does not move status. So with reconciliation off the health projection FREEZES at its last verdict, and a source healthy when the PATCH landed stays healthy forever, keeping the §B.4 reaper guard open indefinitely.\n\nCORRECTION to the issue: oto does not record 'resolved'. sweep.go:246 hard-asserts reaper_would_fabricate_resolution and refuses anything but expired/timeout. The harm is real — a timestamped ending for an alert still firing upstream — but it is an expiry, not a fabricated resolution.","files":null}]}